      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] If the AP resends the `FP_CONTEXT_GET_RESULT` command (e.g., due to a communication timeout or retry loop), this strict check will reject it even if `p-\u003euserid` perfectly matches the already loaded `global_context.user_id`.\n\nConsider allowing the command to succeed if the user ID is unchanged:\n```cpp\nif (fingerprint_auth_enabled() \u0026\u0026\n    (global_context.fp_encryption_status \u0026 FP_CONTEXT_USER_ID_SET) \u0026\u0026\n    memcmp(global_context.user_id.data(), p-\u003euserid, sizeof(global_context.user_id)) !\u003d 0) {\n    return EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED;\n}\n```\nThis preserves the security invariant (preventing cross-user swaps) while making the API more robust to legitimate retries.",
